    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A new AI model developed by the Chinese tech "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "giant",
            "ref": "v-giant"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " ByteDance has recently shaken up Hollywood—not just because of what it can do, but also because of what it might mean for creative industries."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The model is called Seedance 2.0. It can "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "generate",
            "zh": "生成"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " movie-quality videos from just a few written "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "prompts",
            "zh": "提示词"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". These videos even come with sound effects and dialogue. Some clips, featuring popular characters like Spider-Man and Deadpool, quickly went viral."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, Seedance has already run into problems over copyright "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "issues",
            "ref": "v-issue"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This is a growing challenge in the age of AI. Experts warn that AI companies may be putting technology first and people second as they develop more powerful tools and use data without paying for it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Shortly after Seedance was released, major "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "studios",
            "zh": "电影制片厂"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " such as Paramount Pictures sent "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "cease-and-desist letters",
            "zh": "勒令停止函"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to ByteDance. They "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "accused",
            "ref": "v-accuse"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the company of using their content without "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "permission"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The Hollywood actors’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "union",
            "zh": "工会"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", SAG-AFTRA, also "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "criticised",
            "ref": "v-criticise"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the company for its "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "unauthorised",
            "zh": "未经许可的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " use of U.S.-copyrighted works."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Rhett Reese, the co-writer of "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Deadpool & Wolverine"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", reacted strongly after watching a widely shared AI-generated clip of Tom Cruise and Brad Pitt fighting. “It’s likely game over for us,” he said. He added that, soon, one person could sit at a computer and create a movie that looks just like a Hollywood production. “Of course,” he noted, “if that person is no good, the result won’t be great. But if that person has the talent and taste of Christopher Nolan, it could be amazing.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "ByteDance told the BBC that it “respects intellectual "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "property",
            "zh": "知识财产"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " rights and has listened to concerns about Seedance 2.0.” A spokesperson said the company is working to improve safeguards to prevent users from misusing copyrighted content and people’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "likenesses",
            "zh": "肖像"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Meanwhile, for smaller firms, Seedance is too useful to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "ignore",
            "ref": "v-ignore"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". David Kwok from Singapore’s Tiny Island Productions says that AI of this quality could help companies like his create films that would otherwise be far too expensive."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "He gave the example of Asia’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "booming",
            "zh": "飞速发展的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " short-form videos and micro-dramas. Such productions usually have small budgets of about $140,000 for up to 80 two-minute episodes. To save money, companies often focus on family stories because they need fewer special effects. But with AI, Kwok says, creators can aim higher. They could explore "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "genres",
            "zh": "电影类型"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " like science fiction, historical drama, and even action."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
